  "worked_solution": "The change-of-coordinates matrix from $C$ to $B$ is a matrix whose respective columns are the coordinates of the vectors of $C$ relative to the basis $B.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n{P}_{C\\to B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
